  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contribution to UNFPA&apos;s out-of-school CSE project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This programme aimed to operationalize and contextualize the recently released International Technical
Guidance on out of school CSE and support the implementation of out of school national programmes.
The programme has a regional component that will ensure an overall oversight of the intervention,
alignment of the national components with global and regional strategy for out of school CSE,
harmonization of the monitoring framework and evidence generation and dissemination from the
programme.

Marginalized and vulnerable adolescents and young people, in particular young women and girls, have increased access to quality CSE in Burkina Faso, Niger and Chad</narrative>
  </description>
